# Task 218 defense line 4 — LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# RULES:
#   * Every suppression MUST carry a one-line justification.
#   * The suppression count is inventory: it only ever shrinks. A leak that can
#     be released belongs in xr_process_shutdown(), not here.
#   * LeakSanitizer only runs under ASan on Linux. Apple/Homebrew clang on
#     macOS ships ASan WITHOUT a leak detector, so this file is consumed by the
#     lsan_strict lane on Linux CI only (see scripts/run_lsan_strict.sh).
#
# Format: `leak:<substring of a frame's function/file>` (see LSan docs).

# --- Genuinely unreleasable: OS / libc one-time allocations reclaimed at exit.
leak:__cxa_thread_atexit_impl
# ^ glibc thread-local dtor registry; owned by libc, freed by the OS on exit.
leak:dyld
# ^ dynamic loader bookkeeping; not owned by the process.
